{"title":"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Part_1:_Proof_of_Inequality\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Part 1: Proof of Inequality</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Part_2:_Equality_Condition\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Part 2: Equality Condition</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> be an integer and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a29db56a2450439fc073f630d275c66e51a169.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1=d_{1}&lt;d_{2}&lt;d_{3} \\cdots &lt;d_{r}=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"235\" height=\"17\" /> be all of its positive divisors in increasing order. Show that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/2/8e201bb9274ec9bd46a38d9681bf1b22e42d24da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d=d_1d_2+d_2d_3+ \\cdots +d_{r-1}d_r &lt;n^2\\]\" width=\"281\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We proceed with two parts:\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Part_1:_Proof_of_Inequality\">Part 1: Proof of Inequality</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Part 1: Proof of Inequality\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/6/5b6a4b4eb88f996cc9149d546418d83bcc291b2b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{r-1} d_i d_{i+1} = d_1d_2 + d_2d_3 + \\cdots + d_{r-1}d_r\\]\" width=\"304\" height=\"50\" />\nFor each term \\( d_i d_{i+1} \\), note that \\( d_{i+1} \\leq \\frac{n}{d_i} \\) (since divisors come in pairs). Thus:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad616c02edcfe0bf2972476debfd53c30bdcbac3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d_i d_{i+1} \\leq d_i \\cdot \\frac{n}{d_i} = n\\]\" width=\"152\" height=\"35\" />\nSumming over all \\( r-1 \\) terms:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/6/1361ca85d351ddcf327867b03fb6d68143483858.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{r-1} d_i d_{i+1} \\leq (r-1) \\cdot n &lt; n^2\\]\" width=\"219\" height=\"50\" />\nThe last inequality holds because \\( r \\) (the number of divisors) is at most \\( 2\\sqrt{n} \\), making \\( (r-1)n \\leq 2n^{3/2} &lt; n^2 \\) for \\( n &gt; 4 \\). Smaller cases can be verified directly.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Part_2:_Equality_Condition\">Part 2: Equality Condition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Part 2: Equality Condition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Equality occurs **only** when \\( n \\) is prime:\nFor prime \\( n \\), the divisors are \\( 1 \\) and \\( n \\), so:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/6/076b13a4d32cf55b7ef78e841ee78582435b1b69.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d_1d_2 = 1 \\cdot n = n &lt; n^2\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"18\" />\nFor composite \\( n \\), there exists at least one additional divisor \\( d_2 \\) (where \\( 1 &lt; d_2 &lt; n \\)), making the sum strictly larger than \\( n \\) but still less than \\( n^2 \\).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We rewrote the expression so we have to show\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e97fcd1c362d59f82387e1c5e6cdf2d137a4504.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{d_1 d_2} + \\frac{1}{d_2 d_3} + \\cdots + \\frac{1}{d_{k-1} d_k} &lt; 1.\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Then we showed that if two terms of any sequence of the form\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2e04f5ad0cca4c2f296e9ee6a87c195caa9cc35.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{a_1 a_2} + \\frac{1}{a_2 a_3} + \\cdots\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"39\" />\nwhere \\(1 &lt; a_2 &lt; a_3 &lt; \\cdots &lt; a_k\\),\nare of the form \\(d_i = d_{i-1}+1\\) and \\(d_{i+1} = d_i+1\\), then the two terms containing them are maximized.\n</p><p>Next, we showed that if\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/2/062b5916c0e9ebc60adabbf421898ef2259174b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{d_1 d_2} + \\cdots = B,\\]\" width=\"122\" height=\"39\" />\nthen cross multiplying denominators means that \\(k-1\\) terms are multiplied by a term of \\((1+k_1+k_2+\\cdots)\\) whereas \\(k\\) terms are multiplied in the denominator, implying the multiplication of \\((1+k_1+k_2+\\cdots)\\). Thus if the expression is equivalent to \\(B\\), multiplication by \\((1+k_1+\\cdots)\\) yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c5471afe39c7f3f5f19d6f113e871a5d32e4a916.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(1+k_1+k_2+\\cdots)(B-a)}{1+k_1+k_2+\\cdots} + \\frac{a}{k_1+k_2+k_3+\\cdots} = B-a + \\frac{a}{k_1+k_2+k_3+\\cdots},\\]\" width=\"591\" height=\"41\" />\nwhich is minimized if \\(k_1 = k_2 = k_3 = 1\\).\n</p><p>Since we have shown the maximizing configuration for the sequence, we can proceed to show that the infinite sum is maximizing:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/1/621c669dab0aeb49ce42b5a4ea7cbfc9f11f47a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{2 \\cdot 3} + \\frac{1}{3 \\cdot 4} + \\cdots.\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Moreover this sum is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/f/52f084d05c9ac642bac7b662f275cceb1a9d1bc4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[&lt; \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{8} + \\frac{1}{16} + \\cdots &lt; 1,\\]\" width=\"226\" height=\"37\" />\nwhich means the first part is shown.\n</p><p>Finally, for the second part, if\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/a/72a6f08d3b365750df5a03feb8ae9f3e9ec56ba3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{d_1 d_2} + \\frac{1}{d_2 d_3} + \\cdots = \\frac{1}{d_i},\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"39\" />\nthen if \\(d_i &gt; d_2\\) it is impossible. Also if \\(d_i = 1\\) it is impossible from the first part. Thus \\(d_i = d_2\\).\n</p><p>This only works when \\(n\\) is prime, as we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd93f0e8ca37a744b18fc0c06fe2bc30fa87ca37.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{d_2} + \\cdots = \\frac{1}{d_2}\\]\" width=\"106\" height=\"39\" />\nand the ``<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/6/34649241e8a36aac587e902e1445d4a93b014c2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /><i> needs to be zero.</i>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO\" title=\"2002 IMO\">2002 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017053017\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.032 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.094 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 124/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3287/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.414      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.414      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:24633:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017053017 and revision id 291144. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}